From: vyos-ls1046a-build CI <ci@local>
Date: Wed, 02 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fman: port: extend FM_CTL ctrl-params page to O/H ports

0189's "cc_arm" verb failed on real hardware with
fman_pcd_port_ensure_params_page() = -EINVAL. Root cause:
fman_port_set_params_page() unconditionally rejects any port whose
port_type != FMAN_PORT_TYPE_RX -- it was only ever wired for RX ports,
even though the FM_CTL AC 0x28 PRE_BMI_ENQ_FRAME ucode requirement this
page satisfies ("every CC result AD exits through" it, per the existing
comment) is a general CC-dispatch requirement, not RX-specific -- and
0189's cc_arm now arms exactly that dispatch mode (NIA_ENG_HWK|
NIA_KG_CC_EN) on an O/H port for the first time.

The O/H BMI register set already has the exact equivalents of every
register this function touches: fmbm_ogpr (O/H General Purpose
Register, mirrors fmbm_rgpr) and fmbm_ofsdm/fmbm_ofsem (O/H Frame
Status Discard/Error Mask, mirrors fmbm_rfsdm/fmbm_rfsem) -- already
defined in struct fman_port_oh_bmi_regs and already written elsewhere
during O/H bring-up (set_oh_dflt_cfg()). This just completes the
RX-only helper to branch on port_type and use the correct register set;
RX behaviour is byte-identical (same fields, same order, same values).

Verified via ~/kernel-git-cache/linux (canonical, series-through-0189)
+ git apply --check against a fresh HEAD checkout. Board-tested
2026-09-02: cc_arm 0x04 failed with fman_pcd_port_ensure_params_page()
= -22 on the pre-fix image; this is the fix, not yet re-tested.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate | Risk-Tier: A (mechanical extension of
an existing RX-only helper to a second port type using pre-existing
register fields; RX code path unchanged, only a new O/H branch added)
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c | 29 +++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c
index e6f6ef33a060..8ea8bb249010 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_port.c
@@ -2249,7 +2249,7 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(fman_port_get_params_page);
 
 /**
  * fman_port_set_params_page() - program the FM_CTL ctrl-params page (0116)
- * @port:      the FMan RX port
+ * @port:      the FMan RX or O/H port
  * @muram_off: MURAM byte offset of the zeroed 256-byte page
  * @page:      ioremapped virtual address of that page
  *
@@ -2258,22 +2258,42 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(fman_port_get_params_page);
  * FMBM_RGPR = page offset.  Required by the FM_CTL AC 0x28
  * PRE_BMI_ENQ_FRAME ucode that every CC result AD exits through on
  * A006675/SW006 silicon.  Caller zeroes the page.
+ *
+ * T-M6-8 Option D phase 1h: an O/H port arming a CC tree via
+ * fman_port_set_oh_cc_base() needs this same page, since NIA_ENG_HWK|
+ * NIA_KG_CC_EN dispatch also exits through the AC 0x28 ucode -- but the
+ * page setup was only ever wired for RX (fmbm_rfsdm/rfsem/rgpr). The
+ * O/H BMI register set has the exact same fields under different names
+ * (fmbm_ofsdm/ofsem/ogpr, already used elsewhere for O/H bring-up, e.g.
+ * set_oh_dflt_cfg()'s fmbm_ofsdm/ofsem writes) -- this just completes
+ * the RX-only helper to also cover O/H, RX behaviour unchanged.
  */
 int fman_port_set_params_page(struct fman_port *port, u32 muram_off,
 			      void __iomem *page)
 {
 	u32 sdm, sem;
 
-	if (!port || !page || port->port_type != FMAN_PORT_TYPE_RX)
+	if (!port || !page)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	sdm = ioread32be(&port->bmi_regs->rx.fmbm_rfsdm);
-	sem = ioread32be(&port->bmi_regs->rx.fmbm_rfsem);
+	if (port->port_type == FMAN_PORT_TYPE_RX) {
+		sdm = ioread32be(&port->bmi_regs->rx.fmbm_rfsdm);
+		sem = ioread32be(&port->bmi_regs->rx.fmbm_rfsem);
+	} else if (port->port_type == FMAN_PORT_TYPE_OH) {
+		sdm = ioread32be(&port->bmi_regs->oh.fmbm_ofsdm);
+		sem = ioread32be(&port->bmi_regs->oh.fmbm_ofsem);
+	} else {
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
 	iowrite32be(FMAN_PP_MISC_ALWAYS_ON,
 		    (u32 __iomem *)((u8 __iomem *)page + FMAN_PP_MISC_OFF));
 	iowrite32be(sdm | sem,
 		    (u32 __iomem *)((u8 __iomem *)page + FMAN_PP_ERRDISC_OFF));
-	iowrite32be(muram_off, &port->bmi_regs->rx.fmbm_rgpr);
+	if (port->port_type == FMAN_PORT_TYPE_RX)
+		iowrite32be(muram_off, &port->bmi_regs->rx.fmbm_rgpr);
+	else
+		iowrite32be(muram_off, &port->bmi_regs->oh.fmbm_ogpr);
 	port->ctrl_params_page = muram_off;
 
 	dev_info(port->dev,
